  "label": "Survivors are mapped as '3 jewish prisoners after being liberated by the ussr'",
  "description": "The top text overlay explicitly labels the three individuals as '3 jewish prisoners after being liberated by the ussr'. This directly maps the visual entities (the three survivors) onto the textual description, identifying them as Jewish prisoners who were liberated by the USSR. This mapping is central to the meme's intent, as it frames the visual material (the suffering survivors) as a historical event (liberation) and attributes a specific identity ('jewish prisoners') to them, which is contextually significant given the Holocaust context.",
